<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lautaro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1534–1557</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lautaro was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> military leader in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a>. Captured as a youth, he served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a> as a groom and learned Spanish tactics, then escaped and led the Mapuche to victory at Tucapel in December 1553, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdivia">Valdivia</a> was killed. He won further battles and marched north towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, but was killed at Mataquito in 1557.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lautaro.jpg" alt="Lautaro" width="274" height="340" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. GringoInChile assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lautaro_Ca%C3%B1ete.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
